ub.com/repos/elastic/elasticsearch/compare/{base}...{head}","merges_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elastic/elasticsearch/merges","archive_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elastic/elasticsearch/{archive_format}{/ref}","downloads_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elastic/elasticsearch/downloads","issues_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elastic/elasticsearch/issues{/number}","pulls_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elastic/elasticsearch/pulls{/number}","milestones_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elastic/elasticsearch/milestones{/number}","notifications_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elastic/elasticsearch/notifications{?since,all,participating}","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elastic/elasticsearch/labels{/name}","releases_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elastic/elasticsearch/releases{/id}","deployments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elastic/elasticsearch/deployments","created_at":"2010-02-08T13:20:56Z","updated_at":"2026-03-09T09:33:20Z","pushed_at":"2026-03-09T09:33:13Z","git_url":"git://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:elastic/elasticsearch.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch","homepage":"https://www.elastic.co/products/elasticsearch","size":1565901,"stargazers_count":76300,"watchers_count":76300,"language":"Java","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":true,"has_wiki":false,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":false,"forks_count":25807,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":5584,"license":{"key":"other","name":"Other","spdx_id":"NOASSERTION","url":null,"node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTA="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"has_pull_requests":true,"pull_request_creation_policy":"all","topics":["elasticsearch","java","search-engine"],"visibility":"public","forks":25807,"open_issues":5584,"watchers":76300,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elastic/elasticsearch/pulls/112063","html_url":"https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/pull/112063","diff_url":"https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/pull/112063.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/pull/112063.patch","merged_at":"2024-09-13T16:24:34Z"},"body":"In #110830 it was noted that ES|QL produces different results during spatial search for multi-values when we pushdown to lucene versus when we do not. The lucene query understands spatial multi-values, while the compute engine does not.\r\n\r\nNormally ES|QL predicates do not support multi-values because it is ambiguous whether the predicate means `ANY` or `ALL` on the multi-value. For example, if the field `age=[10,30]` and we have the query `FROM index | WHERE age > 20`, it should pass for `ANY` and fail for `ALL`. But in order to answer that, the predicate needs knowledge of this choice between `ANY` and `ALL`.\r\n\r\nIt turns out that this choice is already made for the spatial predicates. They contain knowledge of how to deal with multi-value fields (the choice of `ANY`, `ALL` or some other logic). This is because the spatial types understand the concept of a collection, and already deal with collections, so multi-valued types can be handled naturally. The lucene queries used for lucene-pushdown already support multi-values for spatial predicates like `ST_INTERSECTS`. However, the compute engine does not. The code generated from the `Evaluator` methods explicitly filters out multi-valued fields.\r\n\r\nWhile this PR originally added generic support for multi-value fields using an extension to the `@Evaluator` annotation to explicitly define a combiner (Any vs All combiners), that solution was only sufficient for `ST_INTERSECTS` and `ST_DISJOINT`. It turns out that if the right-hand-side is also compound, then `ST_CONTAINS` and `ST_WITHIN` need more complex support to consider that each of the components of the other parameter needs to be contained or within at least one of the components of the first parameter. For this scenario, it is much simpler to just combined all multi-values into a single parameter before evaluation. For this reason the `@Evaluator` extension was removed in https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/pull/112063/commits/1792442e7338a628b2634b5132815158d6ccb692.\r\n\r\nInstead the solution chosen here was to pass in the parameters as the original Blocks, and rely on the spatial functions to decide how to deal with them (by merging them into single compound geometries before performing the spatial relationship check). The total code complexity is lower. However, if there is interest in supporting the more general Any/All approach to other predicate functions, then reverting the above mentioned commit is one place to consider starting.\r\n\r\nFixes #110830\r\nFixed #112102\r\nFixes #112505 \r\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elastic/elasticsearch/issues/112063/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elastic/elasticsearch/issues/112063/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"id":14251308542,"node_id":"REFE_lADOAAe_f86VTOlNzwAAAANRcbX-","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elastic/elasticsearch/issues/events/14251308542","actor":{"login":"craigtaverner","id":114451,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNDQ1MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/114451?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/craigtaverner","html_url":"https://github.com/craigtaverner","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/craigtaverner/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/craigtaverner/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/craigtaverner/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://